## Coding Standards (project)

- Senior, production-ready, modular, strictly typed Python.
- Change only requested files/functions; no unprompted refactors or dependency bumps.
- No placeholder stubs (`# TODO`, `# implement later`) inside requested scope.
- Zero-assumption: if rounding, NULLs, or edge cases are unclear — **stop and ask**.
- Prefer small targeted diffs over full-file rewrites.
- Money in DB: `NUMERIC`; hot sales loops may use integer kopecks.
- Day-level RNG: derive from `(global_seed, date, store_id)` for reproducible runs.

---

## Non-Goals (v1)

- Multi-warehouse routing (one warehouse for all stores)
- Automatic seed / demo data generation
- Physical delete of stores (use inactive / no delete path as decided)
- ORM / Alembic
- Guessing unspecified business rules
